Task: Direct 2-D conflict test (Phase 4, cmc-2d_20261025)

Added a session-scoped synthetic_xapp fixture factory that trains and caches
max-objective xApps on the four synthetic CSVs, then used it to cover the
direct 2-D conflict between app1 and app2.

- p* must lie inside the per-axis bounding box of the two requested points.
- Both xApps appear in per_xapp in request order.
- Both stay QoS-satisfied at the compromise (2/2 before and after).

Files:
- tests/conftest.py (synthetic fixtures, cached training)
- tests/test_synthetic.py (direct conflict test)

Why: the direct conflict is the basic acceptance case for joint 2-D
bargaining; it must be pinned before the indirect/weight cases build on it.
